}  To read the log and the replies, to give JES2 and operator commands
}  and to purge, SDSF needs the authorized state for a moment. It gets it
}  from an SVC routine of its own, installed with SDSF. Where that is not
}  installed, SDSF uses SVC 244, and only users allowed SVC 244 can do
}  these things. RAKF still decides as above.
}
}  Without the authorized state:
{    COMMAND NOT AUTHORIZED   }for action characters, / commands, PR and
}                             INIT
{    LOG NOT READABLE         }for the log
{    REPLIES NOT READABLE     }for the replies at its end
{    NOT AUTHORIZED           }for P on the Status panel
}
